# Publisher checklist

Complete every unchecked item before submitting EZ Scene Collab.

## Product content

- [x] One clearly named root folder.
- [x] English and Spanish offline documentation.
- [x] Demo scene and prefab that work without ProBuilder.
- [x] Optional ProBuilder demo-object command.
- [x] Changelog, privacy statement, support guide, and third-party notices.
- [x] Add a real maintained product and support URL.
- [x] Add an active support email to the package documentation.
- [ ] Confirm the active support email in the Publisher Portal profile.
- [ ] Add final icon, screenshots, and video links.
- [ ] Review every marketing claim against the final build.

## Validation

- [x] Clean import without ProBuilder, Newtonsoft, or a version-control package.
- [x] ProBuilder 6.0.9 compilation.
- [x] Separate host/client Unity instances on one Windows computer.
- [ ] Two physical Windows computers on a LAN.
- [ ] Two physical Windows computers through Tailscale.
- [ ] Two physical Windows computers through Hamachi if advertised.
- [ ] Public port-forwarding test if documented as supported.
- [ ] Built-in Render Pipeline.
- [ ] URP clean project.
- [ ] HDRP clean project.
- [ ] Every Unity version listed on the store page.
- [ ] macOS and Linux before advertising either one.
- [ ] Large-scene, dense-mesh, reconnect, malformed-data, and multi-user stress tests.
- [ ] Import-over-old-version, uninstall, domain reload, Unity restart, and project reopen.

## Legal and Publisher Portal

- [x] Third-party notices file included.
- [x] Draft AI-assistance disclosure prepared.
- [ ] Verify ownership and licensing of final icon, screenshots, video, demo additions, and marketing assets.
- [ ] Confirm the final Asset Store EULA selection.
- [ ] Complete tax and payout profile.
- [ ] Create the Publisher Portal draft and upload with the current Asset Store Tools.
- [ ] Complete the external listing's dependencies, limitations, privacy, and support fields.
